  ('fp-g00491', 'forest-production', 'forest-biometry-mensuration-inventory', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In a forest inventory, a forester uses a systematic sampling method and chooses sample plots every 200 meters along a transect line. What is an advantage of this systematic sampling approach?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It ensures random selection and minimizes bias"},{"id":"b","text":"It requires fewer samples to achieve high precision"},{"id":"c","text":"It provides better spatial coverage of the forest area"},{"id":"d","text":"It simplifies the calculation of tree density"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00492', 'forest-production', 'forest-biometry-mensuration-inventory', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In forest inventory, what is the primary difference between fixed-area plot sampling and variable-radius plot sampling?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Fixed-area plot sampling is more biased towards larger trees"},{"id":"b","text":"Variable-radius plot sampling does not require any measuring equipment"},{"id":"c","text":"Fixed-area plot sampling involves plots of equal size, while variable-radius plot sampling uses trees'' basal area to determine ''in'' trees"},{"id":"d","text":"Variable-radius plot sampling always results in more trees being counted"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00493', 'forest-production', 'forest-biometry-mensuration-inventory', 'Hard', 'mock',
